 {
  "name": "write-unmatched-can-apply",
  "method": "PATCH",
  "path": "/api/unmatched-jobs/{jobs:26}/status",
  "body": {
   "user_status": "watchlist"
  },
  "after": [
   "/api/unmatched-jobs/{jobs:26}",
   "/api/jobs?status=pending&country=all"
  ],
  "drop_keys": [
   "status",
   "origin",
   "company_profile",
   "job_labels",
   "match_gate",
   "user_status"
  ],
  "drop_keys_why": "Flask returns the raw Mongo posting: status 'unmatched' (no card, so no Tracker status) and origin inferred as 'manual' (a Flask bug). The Unmatched page reads neither. Flask copied only some posting fields to the new card; on Postgres the card shares the posting, so it also shows the gate, labels and company profile."
 },
